        <argsstring>()</argsstring>
        <name>generateWaitCntInfo</name>
        <qualifiedname>llvm::mca::AMDGPUCustomBehaviour::generateWaitCntInfo</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>This method gets called from the constructor and is where we setup the InstrWaitCntInfo vector. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The core logic for determining which CNTs an instruction interacts with is taken from <ref refid="classanonymous__namespace_02_s_i_insert_waitcnts_8cpp_03_1_1_s_i_insert_waitcnts_1a3f5e55facd89c7c4e29803a545e13716" kindref="member">SIInsertWaitcnts::updateEventWaitcntAfter()</ref>. Unfortunately, some of the logic from that function is not available to us in this scope so we conservatively end up assuming that some instructions interact with more CNTs than they do in reality. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
